# compound — A AND B is two sequential guards; there is no `and`/`or` (README
# ss33.4). Prints "both positive" only when a > 0 and b > 0. (todos WS1-068)

Compound is project
Compound module examplesCompound
Compound target console
Compound entry main

examplesCompound is module
examplesCompound path examples.compound
examplesCompound exports main
examplesCompound purpose "Show compound conditions as sequential guards"
examplesCompound invariant "Reaches the both-positive path only when both checks pass"

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32
ExitCode purpose "Process exit status"

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout
stdoutWriter purpose "Allow controlled writes to standard output"

main is operation
main out ExitCode
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memory heap no
main async no
main purpose "Print whether both a and b are positive using sequential guards"
main invariant "The both-positive write is guarded by two ifFalse checks in series"
main let a immutable Int64 3
main let b immutable Int64 4
main let zero immutable Int64 0
main let bothText immutable String "both positive"
main let notBothText immutable String "not both positive"
main let okCode immutable ExitCode 0
main do checkA
main branch ifFalse aPositive goto notBoth
main do checkB
main branch ifFalse bPositive goto notBoth
main do writeBoth
main return okCode
main at notBoth do writeNotBoth
main return okCode

checkA is call
checkA in main
checkA invokes math.greaterThanInt64
checkA arg left Int64 a
checkA arg right Int64 zero
checkA out aPositive Bool

checkB is call
checkB in main
checkB invokes math.greaterThanInt64
checkB arg left Int64 b
checkB arg right Int64 zero
checkB out bPositive Bool

writeBoth is call
writeBoth in main
writeBoth invokes console.writeLine
writeBoth arg text String bothText

writeNotBoth is call
writeNotBoth in main
writeNotBoth invokes console.writeLine
writeNotBoth arg text String notBothText
